  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "/DMrlOauqEQuO76E+pkVM9BHdMs=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:34.956Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "KMD's row lists public sector, pensions and insurance as verticals and records its stack as not researched. The tier came from a mechanical rescore of a provisional v2 tail entry on size and slot occupancy, never from a v3 evidence pass.\n\nSlot occupancy cannot be computed against an empty platform field, so size is the only input that could have produced the do-not-pitch placement. That is a legitimate screen for a Danish firm of KMD's standing, but it is a statement about scale rather than about fit, and the verticals on the row point the other way.\n\nThe flag closes with the same instruction as its neighbours: run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. Until that happens the exclusion and the vertical attractiveness sit side by side on the row without either being resolved.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- KMD (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Public, pensions, insurance",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:31:34.956114Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:34.956119Z"
    }
  },
